   "lines": [
    "Passed my last exam-",
    "ination. I have worked",
    "well these last ten",
    "days; and in fact I",
    "had to. In the after-",
    "noon I drove or[?] in my",
    "cart to the Lees; it was",
    "delightful to get back",
    "to the cheerful house, and",
    "to see kind, hospitable",
    "Mr & Mrs Lee, the pretty",
    "girls and the jolly",
    "little children; and far",
    "more than anything",
    "to be once again with",
    "my own, best beloved",
    "little Queen; I have missed",
    "her so; oh, how sweet",
    "and pretty she was."
   ],
   "rows": null,
   "columns": null,
   "confidence": "high",
   "note": "'or' after 'drove' is as it appears (possibly short for 'over')."
